---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CalcPage from "../../../components/CalcPage.astro";
import TamSamSomCalc from "../../../components/react/TamSamSomCalc";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Step 2: size your market — Calculators"
  description="Calculate TAM, SAM and SOM with a print-vending example. Free data and a street count."
>
  <CalcPage
    lang="en"
    step={2}
    stepName="Size your market"
    lede="How many could buy, how many you reach, how many you win. With your vending as example."
    prevHref={`${base}en/idea-sheet/`}
    prevLabel="Step 1: your sheet"
    nextHref={`${base}en/calculators/product-cost/`}
    nextLabel="Step 3: your cost"
  >
    <div class="rts-panel">
      <h2>What each one is, with your vending</h2>
      <p>One formula for all three: <strong>market = people x pages per person per year x price per page</strong>.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>TAM:</strong> everyone who prints in your city. To locate yourself, not to sell to all.</li>
        <li><strong>SAM:</strong> those who walk by your block: school enrollment plus hospital staff and visitors.</li>
        <li><strong>SOM:</strong> those who actually buy from your machine. This is bottom-up.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="rts-panel">
      <h2>How to get each number</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>People:</strong> ask enrollment at the school and staff at the hospital. Count foot traffic at peak hour. Write it down.</li>
        <li><strong>Pages per person:</strong> use your 5 to 10 talks from step 1. Ask how many pages they print a month. Times 12.</li>
        <li><strong>Price per page:</strong> note what they pay today at the copy shop across the street. That is your ticket.</li>
        <li><strong>TAM in $:</strong> city people x pages x price. Put that $ in the calculator below.</li>
        <li><strong>SAM in %:</strong> which share walks by your block. If your block has 3,000 of 20,000, it is 15%.</li>
        <li><strong>Bottom-up SOM:</strong> pages your machine can sell a day x days a year x price. Compare with the % you set. If they differ, fix the %.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Free sources: business directories for rival copy shops, search trends for demand, plus your street count.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="rts-result">
      <h2>Filled example: your vending</h2>
      <p>Example numbers. Replace with yours.</p>
      <div class="rts-row"><span>TAM</span><strong style="font-size:1rem">20,000 people x 48 pages x $1.50 = $1,440,000 a year</strong></div>
      <div class="rts-row"><span>SAM 15%</span><strong style="font-size:1rem">3,000 on your block x 48 x $1.50 = $216,000</strong></div>
      <div class="rts-row"><span>SOM</span><strong style="font-size:1rem">80 pages a day x 300 days x $1.50 = $36,000 a year</strong></div>
      <p style="margin-top:1rem">In the calculator set TAM = 1,440,000, SAM = 15, SOM = 17. Bottom-up SOM rules: if your machine cannot do 80 pages a day, lower the %.</p>
    </div>

    <TamSamSomCalc lang="en" currency="USD" client:load />

    <div class="rts-panel">
      <h2>Ready to mark done</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>TAM in $ with people, pages and price noted.</li>
        <li>SAM with % that walks by your block.</li>
        <li>SOM checked bottom-up with pages a day.</li>
        <li>Rivals counted by hand on your street.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="rts-papel"><strong>Fills:</strong> market study. SOM feeds step 5 break-even.</p>
    </div>
  </CalcPage>
</BaseLayout>
